From 9f7d575d90b06bbf529b0f20fe759eee65676203 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rishi <rishi@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:36:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add SecretPolicyEngine, typed exceptions, and DELETE
 endpoint

Builds on backend-core's existing entity/repository/service/controller
rather than duplicating them:

- policy/SecretPolicyEngine.java: pulls the status/expiration/password/
  view-limit checks out of SecretService into one focused component
- exception/: 6 typed exceptions + GlobalExceptionHandler, so errors
  return correct 404/410/403 codes with the right reason instead of a
  generic 500
- SecretService: getSecretStatus/accessSecret now delegate to the
  policy engine; added deleteSecret() with management-token validation
- SecretController: added DELETE /api/secrets/{id}
- AccessSecretResponse: added reason field + denied() factory for the
  {"access":"DENIED","reason":"..."} shape from the frozen contract;
  existing 3-arg constructor still works unchanged

Behavior fix: previously, hitting the view limit also set status to
CONSUMED as a side effect. Removed - the frozen contract treats the
view limit as a live comparison (currentViews >= maxViews), not a
stored status, same as how the GET endpoint already checks it.
